      <activity id="fcb99e6a-796b-5c07-844a-e0112262276e" activityNameId="850ee7c6-fcf0-5433-9014-f9bb27b2c58d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, high voltage, consumer, according to BFE 2005, at grid</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, high voltage, consumer, according to BFE 2005, at grid
This dataset describes the transformation from medium to low voltage as well as the distribution of electricity at low voltage.;
UUID: 109ddd62-142d-3dcd-928c-46038ed44171
Included are the electricity production in Abbreviation, the transmission network as well as direct SF6-emissions to air. Electricity losses during low-voltage transmission and transformation from medium-voltage are accounted for.
Location: Data apply to public and self producers. Geographical classification according to IEA. Assumptions for transmission network, losses and emissions are based on Swiss data.
Technology: Average technology used to distribute electricity. Includes underground and overhead lines, as well as air- and SF6-insulated medium-to-low voltage switching stations. Electricity production according to related datasets
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: production volume on low voltage level: 51'000GWh
Sampling: statistics 
Extrapolations: unknown electricity is modeled with UCTE-electricity mix
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_109ddd62-142d-3dcd-928c-46038ed44171.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
